      "side": 1,
      "message": "Gemini generated code. Check for correctness:\n\n----\n\nTo completely decouple the I/O (console printing) from the protocol handler, we need to change `BootromComm::GetBootromInfo()` and `BootromComm::GetFlashInfo()` so that they return populated structs rather than `void`. Then, we shift the responsibility of printing that data up to the application layer.\n\nHere are the exact changes across the files:\n\n### 1. `util/egis/bootrom.h`\n\nUpdate the function signatures to return the structs defined in `EgisBootrom` instead of `void`.\n\n**Current:**\n\n```cpp\n  // --- Basic Bootrom commands ---\n  std::expected\u003cvoid, BootromError\u003e GetBootromInfo();\n  std::expected\u003cvoid, BootromError\u003e GetFlashInfo();\n\n```\n\n**New:**\n\n```cpp\n  // --- Basic Bootrom commands ---\n  std::expected\u003cEgisBootrom::BootromInfoResponse, BootromError\u003e GetBootromInfo();\n  std::expected\u003cEgisBootrom::FlashInfoResponse, BootromError\u003e GetFlashInfo();\n\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. `util/egis/bootrom.cc`\n\nRemove all `std::println` statements. Before returning the struct, normalize the endianness so the application layer doesn\u0027t have to worry about whether the data is little-endian or native-endian.\n\n**Current (`GetBootromInfo`):**\n\n```cpp\nstd::expected\u003cvoid, BootromError\u003e BootromComm::GetBootromInfo() {\n  EgisBootrom::GetBootromInfoCommand req;\n  auto resp \u003d SendStruct(req);\n  if (!resp) return std::unexpected(resp.error());\n\n  auto info_res \u003d ReadStruct\u003cEgisBootrom::BootromInfoResponse\u003e(\n      std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e(*resp));\n  if (!info_res) {\n    return std::unexpected(BootromError::kResponseTruncated);\n  }\n  EgisBootrom::BootromInfoResponse info \u003d info_res.value();\n\n  std::println(\"Bootrom Version: 0x{:x}\", FromLittleEndian(info.version));\n  std::println(\"Max Command Size: {} bytes\",\n               FromLittleEndian(info.max_cmd_size));\n  std::println(\"Max FW Upgrade Size: {} bytes\",\n               FromLittleEndian(info.max_fw_upgrade_size));\n  return {};\n}\n\n```\n\n**New (`GetBootromInfo`):**\n\n```cpp\nstd::expected\u003cEgisBootrom::BootromInfoResponse, BootromError\u003e\nBootromComm::GetBootromInfo() {\n  EgisBootrom::GetBootromInfoCommand req;\n  auto resp \u003d SendStruct(req);\n  if (!resp) return std::unexpected(resp.error());\n\n  auto info_res \u003d ReadStruct\u003cEgisBootrom::BootromInfoResponse\u003e(*resp);\n  if (!info_res) return std::unexpected(BootromError::kResponseTruncated);\n  \n  EgisBootrom::BootromInfoResponse info \u003d info_res.value();\n  \n  // Normalize endianness before returning to the application layer\n  info.version \u003d FromLittleEndian(info.version);\n  info.max_cmd_size \u003d FromLittleEndian(info.max_cmd_size);\n  info.max_fw_upgrade_size \u003d FromLittleEndian(info.max_fw_upgrade_size);\n  \n  return info;\n}\n\n```\n\n**Current (`GetFlashInfo`):**\n\n```cpp\nstd::expected\u003cvoid, BootromError\u003e BootromComm::GetFlashInfo() {\n  std::println(\"--- Fetching Flash Information ---\");\n\n  EgisBootrom::GetFlashInfoCommand req;\n  auto resp \u003d SendStruct(req);\n  if (!resp.has_value()) {\n    std::println(stderr, \"[ERROR] Unable to retrieve Flash info.\");\n    return std::unexpected(resp.error());\n  }\n\n  auto info_res \u003d ReadStruct\u003cEgisBootrom::FlashInfoResponse\u003e(\n      std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e(*resp));\n  if (!info_res) {\n    std::println(stderr, \"[ERROR] Response length insufficient: {}\",\n                 resp-\u003esize());\n    return std::unexpected(BootromError::kResponseTruncated);\n  }\n  EgisBootrom::FlashInfoResponse info \u003d info_res.value();\n\n  std::array\u003cchar, 9\u003e prod_name{};\n  std::memcpy(prod_name.data(), info.prod_name, 8);\n\n  uint32_t flash_size \u003d FromLittleEndian(info.flash_size);\n\n  std::println(\"[SUCCESS] Flash Data Received:\");\n  std::println(\"  Product Name  : {}\", prod_name.data());\n  std::println(\"  Flash Size  : {} bytes ({} MB)\", flash_size,\n               flash_size / 1024 / 1024);\n  return {};\n}\n\n```\n\n**New (`GetFlashInfo`):**\n\n```cpp\nstd::expected\u003cEgisBootrom::FlashInfoResponse, BootromError\u003e\nBootromComm::GetFlashInfo() {\n  EgisBootrom::GetFlashInfoCommand req;\n  auto resp \u003d SendStruct(req);\n  if (!resp) return std::unexpected(resp.error());\n\n  auto info_res \u003d ReadStruct\u003cEgisBootrom::FlashInfoResponse\u003e(*resp);\n  if (!info_res) return std::unexpected(BootromError::kResponseTruncated);\n\n  EgisBootrom::FlashInfoResponse info \u003d info_res.value();\n  \n  // Normalize endianness\n  info.flash_size \u003d FromLittleEndian(info.flash_size);\n  \n  return info;\n}\n\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. `util/egis/et171_flash.cc` (The Caller)\n\nSince the original patch doesn\u0027t actually call `GetBootromInfo()` or `GetFlashInfo()` in its execution path (they appear to be unused or diagnostic), here is how you would consume them in the application layer now that they are decoupled.\n\nYou could add a helper function in `et171_flash.cc` (similar to your existing `ExecuteGetVersion` function):\n\n```cpp\nstd::expected\u003cvoid, BootromError\u003e PrintDeviceDiagnostics(BootromComm\u0026 brom) {\n  std::println(\"\\n--- Fetching Bootrom Information ---\");\n  if (auto info_res \u003d brom.GetBootromInfo(); info_res) {\n    auto\u0026 info \u003d info_res.value();\n    std::println(\"Bootrom Version: 0x{:x}\", info.version);\n    std::println(\"Max Command Size: {} bytes\", info.max_cmd_size);\n    std::println(\"Max FW Upgrade Size: {} bytes\", info.max_fw_upgrade_size);\n  } else {\n    std::println(stderr, \"[ERROR] Failed to get bootrom info: {}\", ToString(info_res.error()));\n  }\n\n  std::println(\"\\n--- Fetching Flash Information ---\");\n  if (auto flash_res \u003d brom.GetFlashInfo(); flash_res) {\n    auto\u0026 flash \u003d flash_res.value();\n    \n    // Safely extract the string\n    std::array\u003cchar, 9\u003e prod_name{};\n    std::memcpy(prod_name.data(), flash.prod_name, 8);\n    \n    std::println(\"[SUCCESS] Flash Data Received:\");\n    std::println(\"  Product Name: {}\", prod_name.data());\n    std::println(\"  Flash Size: {} bytes ({} MB)\", \n                 flash.flash_size, flash.flash_size / 1024 / 1024);\n  } else {\n    std::println(stderr, \"[ERROR] Failed to get flash info: {}\", ToString(flash_res.error()));\n  }\n  \n  return {};\n}\n\n```",
