      "message": "In `util/egis/flasher_logic.cc` (`RunFlashFw`), when you build the dump filename, you use `std::string::substr`:\n\n**Current (`flasher_logic.cc`):**\n\n```c\n  if (config.dump_cmd_fw) {\n    std::ostringstream oss;\n    \n    // This allocates a brand new std::string on the heap just to hold the sub-string\n    std::string fw_filename \u003d config.fw_path.substr(config.fw_path.find_last_of(\"/\\\\\") + 1);\n    \n    std::string algo_tag \u003d (config.algo_type \u003d\u003d EgisCryptoType::kAesGcm) ? \"aes\" : \"sha256\";\n    oss \u003c\u003c fw_filename \u003c\u003c \"_\" \u003c\u003c algo_tag \u003c\u003c \"_cmd_\" \u003c\u003c std::time(nullptr) \u003c\u003c \".bin\";\n    // ...\n\n```\n\n**The Idiomatic C++23 Way:** If you convert the base string to a `std::string_view` first, calling `.substr()` on it returns another lightweight, non-owning view rather than allocating a new string on the heap. `std::ostringstream` natively accepts string views.\n\n```c\n  if (config.dump_cmd_fw) {\n    std::ostringstream oss;\n    \n    // 1. Cast the path to a view\n    std::string_view path_view \u003d config.fw_path;\n    \n    // 2. substr() on a view returns a view (Zero allocations!)\n    auto fw_filename \u003d path_view.substr(path_view.find_last_of(\"/\\\\\") + 1);\n    \n    std::string_view algo_tag \u003d (config.algo_type \u003d\u003d EgisCryptoType::kAesGcm) ? \"aes\" : \"sha256\";\n    oss \u003c\u003c fw_filename \u003c\u003c \"_\" \u003c\u003c algo_tag \u003c\u003c \"_cmd_\" \u003c\u003c std::time(nullptr) \u003c\u003c \".bin\";\n    // ...\n\n```\n\n*(Notice I also changed `algo_tag` from `std::string` to `std::string_view` since it\u0027s just pointing to string literals).*\n\nBy making these changes, you ensure that your code never allocates memory or mutates buffers solely for the purpose of string formatting.",
